  id: W2_05
  era: "c. 335\u2013375 CE"
  title: Gold coin of Samudragupta
  text: "Gold coin of Samudragupta. The Gupta kings issued fine gold coins called dinaras. On this type Samudragupta is shown seated, playing a veena \u2013 a reminder that he was praised as a poet and musician as well as a conqueror. The Gupta period is often called a classical age of Indian art and learning. His achievements are recorded in a long Sanskrit poem carved on the Allahabad pillar, the same pillar that already carried an inscription of Ashoka six hundred years earlier."
